# Block / Page Image Quality (Auto-attach)

When editing block output, kit templates, or demo HTML that includes images:

## Sources
- No `placehold.co`, `via.placeholder.com`, `dummyimage.com`, `picsum.photos`, or broken hotlinks — including in `block.json` `example` and `attributes` defaults
- Prefer WordPress Media Library IDs (`MediaUpload` + `wp_get_attachment_image()`) over hardcoded URLs
- Plugin-shipped art lives under `assets/`; kit demo content under `templates/`
- Confirm licence before any third-party image

## Quality & CLS
- Real, on-brand imagery — not vague stock filler when the product/place/person matters
- Explicit `width`/`height` or CSS `aspect-ratio` to prevent layout shift
- Prefer WebP/optimized sizes; lazy-load below the fold; never lazy-load the LCP image
- Respect the plugin zip budget — new binary assets must not push the release over the size limit

## Accessibility
- Informative images: specific `alt` (editable by the site editor, not hardcoded English)
- Decorative: empty `alt`
- Do not put essential copy only inside an image — text must be a real, translatable attribute

## Checks
- Paths resolve at runtime — use `TWORK_BUILDER_URL` / `plugins_url()`, never a relative path that breaks once installed
- Mobile + desktop crop still readable
- Empty state (no image selected) renders cleanly — no broken-image icon, no stretched placeholder box
